From 5f8f659f07b0fed1dad4df35869b6eb16f6046a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sirius902 <10891979+Sirius902@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:51:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mangoapp: size the window to the output in every layout

33c2c7d removed the branch that shrank the window to the HUD, but left
the horizontal check guarding the resize to the output size. Outside
horizontal mode mangoapp now leaves the window at the 1280x800 it is
created with, and since gamescope composites the external overlay
unscaled from the output origin, every position is confined to the
top-left 1280x800 of a larger output; bottom-right lands near the
middle of a 2560x1440 screen.

Resize in every layout again, keeping the guard against a zero size
from before 378a3b6: msg_read_thread publishes new_frame before it
stores the output size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/app/main.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/app/main.cpp b/src/app/main.cpp
index 551da63..28f571e 100644
--- a/src/app/main.cpp
+++ b/src/app/main.cpp
@@ -332,10 +332,10 @@ static bool render(GLFWwindow* window, overlay_params& real_params) {
     int w, h;
     glfwGetWindowSize(window, &w, &h);
     window_size_changed = w != window_size.x || h != window_size.y;
-    if (real_params.enabled[OVERLAY_PARAM_ENABLED_horizontal])
     // trying to reduce height will break direct scanout in some cases
     // just leave it for now, we'll revisit it in server
-    glfwSetWindowSize(window, screenWidth, screenHeight);
+    if (screenWidth && screenHeight)
+        glfwSetWindowSize(window, screenWidth, screenHeight);
 
     ImGui::EndFrame();
 
-- 
